answer:
Recursion is a programming technique where a function calls itself directly or indirectly to solve smaller sub-problems.

Code:
long factorial(int n) {
    if (n <= 1)
        return 1; // Base condition
    else
        return n * factorial(n - 1); // Recursive call
}

